\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 2.7% Higher; Japan, Libya Remain In Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 21:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 2.7% higher Monday as investors saw promising signs that Japan's nuclear crisis was improving and hoped that U.S. and allied forces' military air strikes in Libya will bring stability back to the oil-rich country.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa increased to 4427.81 points, while volume slipped to 77.5 billion Chilean pesos ($161.3 million) from CLP84.5 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 With appetite for risk improving on the back of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's seemingly easing nuclear crisis and the military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Libya, investors went bargain hunting after seeing the Ipsa drop some 12.5% since the end of December.\par \par \uc2 "Although the outcome is still uncertain, the allied strikes in Libya will likely usher in stability more quickly than would've happened otherwise," said Claudio Gonzalez, head of research at local brokerage Tanner.\par \par \uc2 Also, as several of the Ipsa's heavier weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The DJIA surged 165 points, or 1.4%, to 12023 in late afternoon trade, boosted by a major telecommunications deal and a jump in energy stocks as oil prices leapt.\par \par \uc2 Among gainers, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN), which fell recently after Chile's antitrust court put its proposed merger with Brazilian TAM (TAM, TAMM4.BR) on hold at least until the fourth quarter, rose 1.4% to CLP12,060.00.\par \par \uc2 Compania Sudamericana de Vapores\uc2  (VAPORES.SN) increased 8.2% to CLP273.50 after plummeting in recent weeks as investors fretted about the company's financial health.\par \par \uc2 Power generators also gained, as rains in the nation's southern regions signaled better conditions for hydroelectric power generation. Power producers have seen costs surge, as a drought has curtailed hydroelectric power production.\par \par \uc2 Chile's largest power generator \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN) rose 2% to CLP839.05 and rival \uc2 Colbun (COLBUN.SN) \uc2 jumped 3.5% to CLP124.22.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso ended barely stronger versus the dollar Monday on improved investor sentiment, but pared most of its earlier gains as institutional investors purchased dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at CLP480.50 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP480.80, while trading in a range of CLP479.30 to CLP481.80.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP479.47. It has accumulated $2.70 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in light over-the-counter trading.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.42%, from 2.41% Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.87%, from 2.88% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 21-03-11 2018GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110321e73l0016n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
