\par\par \b \uc2 G-7  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Is Symbolic Tempering Of Markets, Not Targeting Of Yen Level-Economists\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ian Talley and Michael R. Crittenden  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 887 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 23:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Group of Seven's coordinated efforts Friday to weaken the value of the Japanese yen are likely designed more to temper panicked markets than targeting a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, economists say.\par \par \uc2 That should help markets to determine how much--or little--further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be coming in the days and weeks ahead.\par \par \uc2 "This is a short-term measure that has more the goal of stabilization and averting a short-run panic than taking a view about how global imbalances might evolve and what the right value of the yen is against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ralph Bryant, a former director of the Federal Reserve's international finance division, now a fellow at the Brookings Institute.\par \par \uc2 The G-7 overnight sold yen under an agreed so-called coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying, "excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates have adverse implications for economic and financial stability," and that they will monitor exchange markets closely.\par \par \uc2 The yen late Wednesday popped against the dollar to the strongest historical level, battering an economy already devastated by a catastrophe. A devastating 9.0 magnitude earthquake and ensuing tsunami ruined cities and villages in northern Japan last Friday. Japanese authorities raised the death toll Thursday to 5,457, with an additional 9,508 missing, though the numbers are expected to climb.\par \par \uc2 The strong yen's immediate impact--with the Nikkei plummeting--and the long-term potential to disrupt the country's return to health, as well as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility's ability to disrupt global trade, spurred officials to move decisively Thursday at the request of Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "This kind of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...has signaled pretty clearly that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wide awake and it not only is committed to but has the support of its G-7 partners to do whatever it takes to prevent the yen from moving in the wrong direction," said Barry Eichengreen, a University of California, Berkeley, economist.\par \par \uc2 The G-7's surprise joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlike previous G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say Nomura Securities \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts. "Typically in the past, when the G-7 has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a coordinated fashion, it has been because the exchange rate in question was dramatically misaligned," Jens Nordvig, Global Head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy said in a client call. In 2000, the group's goal was not only to stabilize the euro, but to reverse the weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's longer-term trend. That was also the case in 1995, when the goal was to strengthen the dollar. "If you look at where the yen is in real effective terms, it is not dramatically away from historical averages," he said.\par \par \uc2 And if the goal was to indicate to the market that the G-7 was prepared to battle against any strengthening beyond pre-quake levels, then it may be that the G-7 communique is as powerful as the actual yen selling.\par \par \uc2 "If the message is believed then you don't have to actually see the action...The symbolism of the coordinated action is what is most important right now," said Cornell University economist Eswar Prasad. "But they could hit it a lot harder\u8230\'20\'26that's what gives them the confidence to make the strong statement that they did."\par \par \uc2 Bryant said that if there isn't much more disruptive behavior in the financial markets and the yen market in particular, "I wouldn't be surprised if they don't do very much more...Maybe some of the desired effects have been accomplished already through the signalling," he said.\par \par \uc2 Nomura Securites' Nordvig said that while G-7 countries are likely to be comfortable with a range near prequake levels around 83 yen against the dollar, beyond that, members may disagree over the appropriate level of strength. Markets are estimating the Japanese have sold around 2 trillion yen Friday, about the same amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  they did to limited success unilaterally in September. The Fed confirmed it also sold yen Friday, but the U.S. has limited abilities: its yen reserves total around 2 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2 James Pearson, global head of Nomura's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading desk in London said, regardless of what amounts the U.S. Fed or the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  contribute, he thinks there's "considerable amount" more to expect from the Japanese next week. "This is a once-in-a-decade event, it's a rare opportunity for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to galvanize and garner support of the international community," he said, adding, "If they can stabilize and reverse the yen...you could see the yen moving into JPY80 to JPY85 range."\par \par \uc2 Friday afternoon, the yen traded round 80.65 yen to the dollar. That's compared to the record JPY76-level Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 But, Bryant cautions, "who knows what the hell the next news is going to be about the nuclear reactors." If the radiation situation deteriorates further, it could cause further panic in the markets, putting pressure on the yen again. "That would be the kind of circumstance where they would be ready to cooperate again with more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 By Ian Talley and Michael R. Crittenden, 202-862-9285; ian.talley@dowjones.com [ 03-18-11 1829ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110318e73i001ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
