\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOJ's Current Account As Large As During QE In Early 2000s\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 09:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --BOJ's current account balance is expected to increase in size to as large as during quantitative easing in early 2000s\par \par \uc2 --BOJ offers Y1 trillion same-day funds in afternoon, following Y3 trillion in morning\par \par \uc2 --The move comes in tandem with joint action by Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts to weaken the yen\par \par \uc2 (Adds details of BOJ's current account balance and afternoon \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Megumi Fujikawa \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of Japan's current account is expected to expand in size to as large as it was when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  implemented its quantitative-easing policy in the early-2000s, as it continued to aggressively provide emergency funds Friday to calm markets unnerved by last week's massive earthquake and the ensuing nuclear power crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For a fifth straight day, the BOJ offered same-day funds, to the tune of Y3 trillion Friday morning, of which financial firms took up Y1.677 trillion. The bank announced an additional Y1 trillion later in the day, with Y300 billion in bids. Providing same-day funds effectively makes money available immediately to cash-strapped financial companies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ's current account balance--a measure of deposits placed by financial firms with the BOJ--is expected to reach around Y33.2 trillion Friday, based on the bank's previous balance forecast and the day's same-day \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results. That would make the balance the largest since Feb. 24, 2006, when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the late stages of its quantitative-easing program.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An expansion in the balance "mainly reflects the effort to stabilize the money market. However, in our view, it can also be regarded as preemptive unsterilization" of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ's fund injection comes in tandem with joint action by Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The yen hit an all-time high early Thursday morning in Asian time at Y76.25 against the U.S. dollar, posing a threat to Japan's export-driven economy, which is already burdened by the impact of the quake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A person familiar with the BOJ's thinking told Dow Jones Newswires Friday that "the bank will continue ample liquidity provision, along with yen funds injected via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Since the bank has already supplied plenty of funds, it would be difficult to distinguish which money is increased via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but (the bank's stance to keep providing liquidity) could consequently make" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized, the person added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say leaving the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized would make the finance ministry's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more effective in pushing down the yen as it makes monetary conditions in the domestic markets even more accomodative.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been flooding the short-term money market with liquidity since Monday as last week's massive earthquake, devastating 10-meter tsunami and an ensuing nuclear crisis heightened concerns about the ability of banks to meet a surge in demand for funds from companies and households.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid increasing downside risks from the quake and the yen's appreciation, Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made its easy-policy stance clear to market participants.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOJ Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said in an emergency statement issued Friday morning that "the Bank of Japan will pursue powerful monetary easing and, to ensure stability in financial markets, will continue to provide ample liquidity."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday include the buying of Y2 trillion of Japanese government bonds via a reverse repurchase agreement and purchases of Y150 billion treasury discount bills via its asset-purchase program, which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this week doubled the size of to Y10 trillion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It also offered Y2 trillion of two-week funds and Y3 trillion of 1.5-month loans in the afternoon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com [ 03-18-11 0435ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110318e73i0001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
