\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par FED COMPLETES STRESS TESTS OF 19 LARGEST US BANKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed says it completed a new round of tests on the financial health of the 19 largest U.S. banks, and several of the banks rushed to announce they were returning capital to shareholders through dividend increases or share buybacks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LIBYA RENEWS ATTACKS AFTER CEASE-FIRE OFFER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya's foreign minister says the country will abide by the United Nations Security Council resolution calling for military action in Libya, and will implement an immediate cease-fire and end all military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  across the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; BUYS DOLLARS AND SELLS YEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, buying dollars and selling yen as part of a coordinated effort by Group of Seven nations to weaken Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S FUKUSHIMA 1 SITUATION NOT DETERIORATING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The tense situation at Japan's earthquake-hit Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant hasn't deteriorated in the past 48 hours, but the incident has now been identified as a level five accident, the United Nations' nuclear watchdog says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS UP ON DIVIDEND NEWS, CALMER GEOPOLITICS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks climb as fears of increased violence in Libya scale back, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  help relieve pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy and a handful of U.S. companies raise their dividends.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEC CHARGES IBM WITH BRIBING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEC charges IBM with bribing South Korean and Chinese government officials with cash payments, gifts and travel, according to documents filed in federal district court in Washington.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LIBERTY GLOBAL CLOSES IN ON GERMAN CABLE TV BUY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 John Malone\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberty Global\f28 \uc2 \f2  is closing in on a deal to buy Kabel Baden-Wuerttemberg, Germany's third-largest cable TV company, for 3.1 billion euros to 3.2 billion euros ($4.5 billion), people familiar with the matter say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DIPS AS LIBYA EYES TRUCE, BUT FIGHTING PERSISTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude prices fall after Libyan forces called a cease-fire, but reports of renewed fighting on the ground and the mobilization of Western forces raise doubts the conflict will end soon. Nymex April crude ends down 35c at $101.07 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FEDEX FACES PROBE ALONGSIDE UPS OVER CONSULTANTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The package shipper says in a regulatory filing that the justice department last month asked it to provide information "into the policies and practices of \f28 \uc2 \f2 FedEx\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Parcel Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  for dealing with third-party consultants."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YANKEE BOND ISSUANCE HITS RECORD HIGH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign borrowers have tapped U.S. investors at record rate in 1Q, seeking to refinance mountains of maturing debt while taking advantage of artificially low interest rates on this side of the Atlantic. So far this year, $206 billion of "Yankee bonds" were issued, according to Dealogic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Sports \par TEXAS, MICHIGAN, NOTRE DAME WIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Texas tops Oakland 85-81 and Michigan defeats Tennessee 75-45. No. 2 seed Notre Dame also wins, defeating Akron 69-56. Villanova clings to a small lead over George Mason in the second half.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Taking Stock \par WATCH FOR TIMING WHEN MAKING DIVIDEND PLAYS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tomi Kilgore says dividends can be a touchy subject on Wall Street. Everyone knows it is a good sign when a company has fundamental fortitude to initiate or raise its dividend. But they also know it doesn't guarantee outperformance, much less actual gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed Watch \par FED HAS LIMITED YEN WAR CHEST FOR MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Michael S. Derby says the Federal Reserve's contribution to a global effort to weaken the yen is limited by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's war chest of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -like assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par YEN FOR JAPANESE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY FADE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yen strength may prove fleeting, even without ongoing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . David Reilly explains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS GAIN, BUT TRADERS REMAIN CAUTIOUS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks climb higher after news of Libya cease-fire, G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and dividend hikes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS FALL, BUT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , MIDDLE EAST FEARS FUEL RALLY ON WEEK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys fall for the day, but Japan, Middle East fears fuel rally on week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO HITS SESSION HIGHS VS DOLLAR; DOLLAR BELOW Y81 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro hits session high against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DIPS AS LIBYA EYES TRUCE, BUT FIGHTING PERSISTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures fall as Libya calls a cease-fire although reports of fighting persist.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEOPOLITICAL HEADWINDS LIFT GOLD PRICES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comex gold rises, lifted by investor demand for a safe haven. [ 18-03-11 2100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i001cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
