\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par FED COMPLETES STRESS TESTS OF 19 LARGEST US BANKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't disclose the test results and doesn't say which institutions were granted permission to increase dividends. The Fed says it will discuss the tests with banks Friday and present them with a more detailed review later this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LIBYA DECLARES CEASE-FIRE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya's foreign minister says the country will abide by the United Nations Security Council resolution calling for military action in Libya, and will implement an immediate cease-fire and end all military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  across the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; BUYS DOLLARS AND SELLS YEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, buying dollars and selling yen as part of a coordinated effort by Group of Seven nations to weaken Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO RADIATION TAD HIGHER THAN NORMAL, IAEA TO MEASURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Radiation levels in the Tokyo area are around typical background levels, while in areas close to the quake-damaged Fukushima nuclear power plant they remain high but still below levels that would pose a threat to human health, officials say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS CLIMB AS GLOBAL TURMOIL SCALES BACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rose Friday as Libya declared a cease-fire in the wake of a NATO decision to enforce a no-fly zone there, and a G-7 coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped send the yen lower, relieving pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HIKES BANKS RESERVE RATIO FOR THIRD TIME THIS YEAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says it will raise the share of deposits banks must hold in reserve by 0.50 percentage points, the third hike this year, as inflationary pressures remain in the spotlight.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL ERASES LOSSES ON LIBYA CEASE-FIRE DOUBTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil prices are nearly flat on doubts about Libya's declaration of an immediate cease-fire. Nymex April crude is up 2c at $101.44 a barrel after falling as low as $100.32 earlier after the cease-fire was ordered.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN BANK GROUPS CRITICIZE STRESS TEST'S PLANNED CAPITAL RULES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two groups representing German banks criticize plans by European regulators to use a tighter capital definition in this year's stress testing exercise for European banks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENAULT SECURITY AGENT NAMES SOURCE FOR ESPIONAGE CLAIM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Renault security employee has divulged the name of a person he says is the informer that prompted that car maker to believe it had been the victim of industrial espionage, the Paris prosecutors' office says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN TRADING DESK CUTS PART OF ANNUAL 5% CULLING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 's plan to hire for its investment management division and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in fast-growing foreign markets like China doesn't mean it has put a stop to an annual ritual that culls the lower 5% of its staff.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Sports \par TEXAS-OAKLAND KICK OFF DAY 2 OF NCAA TOURNEY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Second day of the NCAA tournament kicks off with Texas vs. Oakland and Tennessee vs. Michigan. 13th-seeded Morehead State and 12th-seeded Richmond lead upsets on Day 1.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interview \par NUCLEAR FEARS MAY GIVE GREENS FIRST STATE PREMIER IN GERMANY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fears about nuclear energy after Japan's catastrophe may give Germany's Green Party their first taste of state leadership in March 27 elections in the key state of Baden-Wuerttemberg, if a new poll proves correct.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Focus \par JAPAN MAY HAVE HAD LITTLE TO DO WITH CHINA'S MOVE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's decision to raise reserve requirements for the sixth time has once again given conspiracy theorists plenty to play with, coming only hours after the G-7 launched a coordinated exercise to weaken Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , writes Nicholas Hastings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS CLIMB AS GLOBAL TURMOIL SCALES BACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks continue to rise after news of a Libya cease-fire, G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS PARE LOSSES; VOLATILE TRADE TO PERSIST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys pare losses in volatile trading with many investors staying on the sidelines.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR RESUMES RISE AGAINST YEN; CLIMBS BACK ABOVE Y81 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar regains footing against the yen, rising to above Y81.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FLAT AS CEASEFIRE DOUBTS SURFACE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures are nearly flat, paring losses on doubts about Libya cease-fire.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD OFF HIGHS ON LIBYA CEASEFIRE; EYES DOLLAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold pares gains after Libya cease-fire news. [ 18-03-11 1600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0016m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
