\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/Japan Real Time: Quick Read: Latest Japan News at a Glance\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 15:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Japan Real Time Report blog at blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime.)\par \par \uc2 The latest news from Japan at a glance:\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR AGENCY: FUKUSHIMA AS BAD AS THREE MILE ISLAND\par \par \uc2 The accident at the Fukushima plant now ranks alongside the 1979 accident at Three Mile Island in terms of scale, Japan's nuclear-safety agency said Friday. The agency raised the accident rating to level five from four after considering the suspected extent of damage to fuel at the plant's reactors.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese Self Defense Force finished its water-cooling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  using water cannons and fire trucks. Seven trucks trained water on Reactor No. 3, which is thought to present the greatest immediate danger. An SDF official said radiation levels were low enough not to present a health risk to SDF members conducting the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Naoto Kan pledged to disclose as much information as possible on the crisis to the international community during his meeting Friday with International Atomic Energy Agency Chief Yukiya Amano. He said an agency team will be dispatched "within a couple of days" to monitor radiation levels in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 PROGRESS MADE IN RECONNECTING POWER AT STRICKEN PLANT\par \par \uc2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Yukio Edano said progress was being made to reconnect power at the stricken plant. Restoring electricity to the reactor's cooling systems could represent the major breakthrough needed for bringing the crisis at the plant under control. A nuclear safety agency official said Reactors No. 1 and No. 2 would be reconnected first, within the day, while Reactor No. 3 wouldn't get power until as late as Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Japan's top government official reiterated that cooling Reactor No. 3 remained the main priority, since it is believed that spent fuel in a tank at the reactor is exposed, presenting a high radiation risk.\par \par \uc2 TOKYO RADIATION A TAD HIGHER THAN NORMAL, STILL NEGLIGIBLE\par \par \uc2 Radiation levels in the Tokyo area were around typical background levels on Friday afternoon, while in areas close to the quake-damaged Fukushima nuclear power plant they remained high but still below levels that would pose a threat to human health, officials said. A top SDF official said Friday that radiation levels at Fukushima are low enough to ensure the safety of the members at the scene.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped massive quantities of yen Friday, aiming to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record surge from further damaging the country's economy.\par \par \uc2 In an extraordinary trading session in Europe, several European central banks were seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to tame the yen. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bundesbank, the Bank of France, the Bank of England and later the Bank of Italy came after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also confirmed that it had participated in selling the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u194\'00\'C2 The Federal Reserve and the \uc2 Bank of Canada\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, buying dollars and selling yen as part of the coordinated effort.\par \par \uc2 ASIAN SHARES FINISH MOSTLY HIGHER\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei Stock Average ended at 9206.75, up 2.7% for the day but still down more than 10% for the week. Among the big stock movers, \uc2 Taiheiyo Cement Corp\uc2 . climbed 15%, \uc2 JFE Holdings Inc\uc2 . added 3.6%, \uc2 Toshiba Corp\uc2 . rose 7.5% and \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  Co. jumped 6.4%.\par \par \uc2 SONY: SIX MANUFACTURING PLANTS IN JAPAN STILL OFFLINE\par \par \uc2 Japan's \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2 . said Friday six of its manufacturing plants that make various devices and components, including Blu-ray discs and lithium-ion batteries, remain closed following the massive earthquake and tsunami that struck the country last week. \u194\'00\'C2 \uc2 Honda Motor Co\uc2 . said Friday that it will continue to suspend automobile and motorcycle assembly \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 18-03-11 1429GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0014g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
