\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TAMES YEN, BUT LITTLE FURTHER WEAKNESS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen edges higher in London trading hours, despite European central banks stepping in to sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of coordinated action by the G7 to stabilize the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after its recent record surge.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FACES MISTRUST AS NUCLEAR EFFORTS CONTINUE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan reports continued modest progress in its efforts to keep under control the stores of nuclear waste at Fukushima Daiichi nuclear facility, although the US signals distrust of the reports, setting up its own channels of information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES GAIN FURTHER AFTER G-7 ACTION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures add to their gains after the Group of Seven agrees to take coordinated action to halt the yen's surge in the wake of last week's earthquake in Japan, while investors monitor efforts to bring a damaged nuclear plant under control.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UN SECURITY COUNCIL ENDORSES LIBYA NO-FLY ZONE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The United Nations Security Council authorizes military force against Libyan leader Moammar Gadhafi's security forces, opening the way for European and American airstrikes on the North African country within the coming days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HIKES BANKS RESERVE RATIO FOR THIRD TIME THIS YEAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says it will raise the share of deposits banks must hold in reserve by 0.50 percentage points, the third hike this year, as inflationary pressures remain in the spotlight.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL BRIEFLY TURNS NEGATIVE ON CHINA RATIO HIKE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude futures dip into negative territory after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its reserve requirement ratio, but quickly regained lost ground as market focus remains locked on developments in Libya.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN REPORTEDLY CUTS 5% OF TRADING DESK STAFF \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut 5% of its trading desk staff as part of its annual review process, Reuters reports. Other divisions were also affected by layoffs, according to the report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED POISED TO EASE ITS GRIP ON BANKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve expects to free some of the nation's biggest banks from strict oversight, for the first time since the government propped up the industry as it threatened to collapse more than two years ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUTCHISON PORT DEBUTS DOWN 6% IN SINGAPORE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Port Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  makes a lackluster debut on the Singapore Exchange, falling 6% below its initial public offer price in the largest ever listing in Singapore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPENDING BILL PASSES, NPR TARGETED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Senate approves legislation to fund the government for three more weeks, amid bipartisan hopes that it would be the last short-term spending bill needed for the current fiscal year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Sports \par GONZAGA UPSETS ST. JOHN'S; MOREHEAD STUNS LOUISVILLE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Demonte Harper made a 3-pointer from the top of the circle with 4.2 seconds left Thursday to lead 13th-seeded Morehead State to the first upset of the NCAA tournament, a 62-61 victory over No. 4 Louisville in the Southwest regional.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Morning Briefing \par G-7 ACTION TO SPUR STOCKS HIGHER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks are expected to open higher, comforted by the G-7 agreement to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stem the yen's rise and support the Japanese economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par FOR OBAMA, A TWO-FRONT BATTLE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama faces the prospect of striking against Libya at a time when lawmakers are preoccupied with budget deficits and, in some cases, expressing reluctance to take part in another war.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Taking Stock \par JAPANESE STOCKS WERE TOUTED AS CHEAP BEFORE... \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before the earthquake hit, there were plenty of people who thought Japanese stocks were on offer at bargain-basement prices. Even if you didn't fully agree back then, what about now? David Cottle writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES HIGHER AFTER G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures gain further after G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS REBOUND; LIBYA, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TRUMP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys rebound as Libya, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's nuclear situation trump \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEANS DIVE INTO G-7 YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Te Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regains momentum and claws back losses following a series of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL BRIEFLY TURNS NEGATIVE ON CHINA RATIO HIKE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude futures dip after China raises its reserve requirement ratio, market focus locked on Libya\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD HIGHER AS OIL RISES, MARKETS EYE LIBYA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold is trading almost 1% higher in Europe as the price of oil rises. [ 18-03-11 1300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0011q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
