\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 960 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 09:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par G-7 PLEDGES RARE JOINT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS CRISIS-STRICKEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SELLS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped yen on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Friday to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's record surge from further damaging an economy ravaged by earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disaster. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HAS SET NO LIMIT ON SIZE OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Ministry has no pre-set limit on the amount of yen it may sell through market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the matter said Friday, underscoring its resolve to prevent the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from rising sharply verus the dollar and other key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0709 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH RATINGS SAYS BOJ ACTIONS CONSTRUCTIVE FOR JAPAN ECON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings said Friday the Bank of Japan's actions to buy in full Y10 trillion in reconstruction bonds will help the country's economic recovery folowing a the devastating earthquake and tsunami that triggered a nuclear crisis in one of the country's atomic power plants. (published 0710 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: UN SECURITY COUNCIL ENDORSES NO-FLY ZONE IN LIBYA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The United Nations Security Council authorized military force Thursday against Libyan leader Moammar Gadhafi's security forces, opening the way for European and American airstrikes on the North African country within the coming days. (published 2306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN FEBRUARY PPI +0.7% ON MONTH, +6.4% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Producer prices in Germany, Europe's largest economy, rose at a faster pace on the year in February largely as a result of higher energy prices, although the monthly increase in prices slowed, the Federal Statistics Office said Friday. (published 0717 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: NATIONS ACT TO PUT BRAKES ON YEN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's economic powerhouses banded together in an attempt to tame an unwelcome rise in the value of the Japanese yen--a development that had threatened to handicap Japan's recovery from the recent devastating earthquake and tsunami. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ OFFERS Y3 TLN SAME-DAY FUNDS TO EASE QUAKE FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan offered to inject another Y3 trillion in same-day funding Friday morning to calm jitters in the markets due to the massive earthquake and subsequent nuclear power crisis, marking a fifth straight day of the bank's emergency action. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: BOJ TO CONTINUE TO PROVIDE AMPLE LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to pump cash into Japan's financial system as needed to stabilize domestic financial markets as Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts act jointly to stabilize \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF ENGLAND'S DEPUTY GOVERNOR AGAINST IMMEDIATE RATE RISE -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britain has entered a hazardous period as new question marks hang over the domestic economy's recovery at a time of persistently above-target inflation, a top Bank of England official said, The Times in London reported Friday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE CONTINUES TO EVAPORATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumers became even more pessimistic about the outlook for the economy and their job prospects during February, and less willing to spend, according to a monthly survey commissioned by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nationwide Building Society\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA OFFICIAL: AIM TO RAISE 58%-64% OF NEXT FISCAL YEAR BORROWING IN APRIL-SEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government aims to raise between 58% and 64% of its borrowing for the next fiscal year in the April-September period, a senior finance ministry official said Friday. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FEWER CHINESE CITIES POST HIGHER NEW HOME PRICES IN FEBRUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices of newly built residential properties in 56 of the 70 large and medium-sized Chinese cities covered by a survey rose in February from the previous month, a slight improvement from January, indicating a partial success in the government's effort to bring stubbornly high home prices under control. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC PROFESSOR: CHINA NEEDS TO LOWER NET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PURCHASES TO CONTROL INFLATION - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China needs to effectively lower the massive amount of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  it buys to rein in inflation, a professor at a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  training institute said in an opinion piece published Friday in the state-run Shanghai Securities News. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: EBA: EU STRESS TESTS WILL FOCUS ON BANKS' CORE TIER 1 CAPITAL LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European officials unveiled some details of the "stress tests" they plan to run on the continent's banks, hoping to show that the exercise will be tough enough to defuse fears about the sector's health. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS TO WEAKEN FURTHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: More bear pressure is likely to emerge on Friday, to close the small upside gap at 122.63. Wednesday's peak at 123.92 is likely to become a significant short-term peak, and there is scope for more weakness to the Mar. 14 higher low at 121.70. A head-and-shoulders top formation is appearing on the 60-minute chart, which will look to limit upside risk to 123.69. (published 0705 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR/USD SET FOR MORE GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Further gains are expected above 1.4088 as the powerful two-month uptrend threatens to extend. A wave equality target lies at 1.4125, but there is scope for 1.4165 based on the recent intraday higher low at 1.3980. Sterner resistance lies at the top end of the monthly Ichimoku cloud at 1.4185. Congestion between 1.3980 and 1.4036 will attract support, and only below the latter would concern USD bears. (published 0710 GMT) [ 18-03-11 0827GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument D