\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For March 18\b0\par\par\uc2 2,042 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: NATIONS ACT TO PUT BRAKES ON YEN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's economic powerhouses banded together in an attempt to tame an unwelcome rise in the value of the Japanese yen--a development that had threatened to handicap Japan's recovery from the recent devastating earthquake and tsunami. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ OFFERS Y3 TLN SAME-DAY FUNDS TO EASE QUAKE FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan offered to inject another Y3 trillion in same-day funding Friday morning to calm jitters in the markets due to the massive earthquake and subsequent nuclear power crisis, marking a fifth straight day of the bank's emergency action. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ SHIRAKAWA: BOJ TO CONTINUE TO PROVIDE AMPLE LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to pump cash into Japan's financial system as needed to stabilize domestic financial markets as Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts act jointly to stabilize \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA OFFICIAL: AIM TO RAISE 58%-64% OF NEXT FISCAL YEAR BORROWING IN APRIL-SEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government aims to raise between 58% and 64% of its borrowing for the next fiscal year in the April-September period, a senior finance ministry official said Friday. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: FEWER CHINESE CITIES POST HIGHER NEW HOME PRICES IN FEBRUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices of newly built residential properties in 56 of the 70 large and medium-sized Chinese cities covered by a survey rose in February from the previous month, a slight improvement from January, indicating a partial success in the government's effort to bring stubbornly high home prices under control. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC PROFESSOR: CHINA NEEDS TO LOWER NET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PURCHASES TO CONTROL INFLATION - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China needs to effectively lower the massive amount of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  it buys to rein in inflation, a professor at a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  training institute said in an opinion piece published Friday in the state-run Shanghai Securities News. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BERNANKE, TRICHET FIRST AMONG G-7 CENTRAL BANKERS SAYING WOULD HELP IN YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to curb the value of the yen was unanimously backed by all members of the Group of Seven industrialized nations, with U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet the first in expressing their support for the coordinated move, a G-7 official told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN YOSANO: BOJ WON'T BE ASKED TO TAKE SPECIAL STEPS ON ANY RECONSTRUCTION-RELATED BONDS -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano said Friday that the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't be called upon to take special steps such as underwriting any earthquake reconstruction government bonds, after a local media report earlier in the day said Tokyo had decided on such an option, the Nikkei reported. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: BEHIND YEN'S RECORD SURGE; INDIVIDUAL INVESTORS, HEDGE FUNDS SCRAMBLED TO BUY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A day after a heart-stopping rally drove the Japanese yen to one of its sharpest ascents in history, traders and bankers blamed a freak onslaught of forced buying by Japanese individual investors and hedge funds--a barrage that came at the exact time of day when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is at its most vulnerable. (published 2326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN GOVERNMENT SUPPORTS RISE IN MINIMUM WAGE - TREASURER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government will support a pay increase for the nation's lowest-paid workers, with the rise to be consistent with increases in the cost of living and other economic changes, Treasurer Wayne Swan said Friday. (published 0502 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI MINISTRY: FEBRUARY CUSTOMS-BASIS TRADE SURPLUS $1.77 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand swung back to a trade surplus of $1.77 billion in February from the previous month's deficit of $857 million, the Ministry of Commerce said Friday. (published 0631 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAI COMMERCE MIN: JAPAN DISASTER AFFECTING THAI EXPORTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai exporters are being affected by the Japan disaster, with some unable to deliver goods because of the closure of some ports, Commerce Minister Porntiva Nakasai said Friday. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES FEB BALANCE OF PAYMENTS DEFICIT WIDENS TO $133 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines recorded a balance of payments deficit of $133 million in February, wider than the $125 million posted in the year-earlier period, data released by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday showed. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: DEVELOPMENT BANK OF THE PHILIPPINES PLANS INTERNATIONAL BOND WORTH UP TO $300M - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Development Bank of the Philippines\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to sell a 10-year dollar-denominated international bond today worth up to $300 million, people familiar with the proposed deal said Friday. (published 0434 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TOKYO SHARES UP 1.8% AS YEN FALLS ON G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo stocks trimmed early gains made after the Group of Seven jointly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, pushing down the value of the yen, but the benchmark Nikkei Stock Average was still up 1.8% at the interval as the earthquake-ravaged nation took comfort from the coordinated G-7 action. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SONY: 6 MANUFACTURING PLANTS IN JAPAN HAVEN'T RESUMED PRODUCTION AS OF FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday six of its manufacturing plants that make various devices and components, including Blu-ray discs and lithium-ion batteries, remain closed following the massive earthquake and tsunami that struck the country last week. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: HONDA UNSURE WHEN JAPAN PLANTS WILL RETURN TO FULL PRODUCTION - MEMO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has warned U.S. dealers that it is not sure if it will be able to resume full production at certain Japanese plants before May, a sign the auto industry may face greater disruption due to the earthquake and tsunami than previously feared. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SAMSUNG EXPECTS RECORD 2011 PROFIT DESPITE TOUGH CONDITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects to return a record operating profit in 2011 even though trading conditions will remain difficult as intensifying competition among electronics companies and global economic headwinds will put pressure on margins. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: BOEING SAYS FUTURE PART SHORTAGES POSSIBLE FROM JAPANESE SUPPLIERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While monitoring the ongoing crises in Japan, officials from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Thursday said they are determining how to deal with possible airplane parts shortages from suppliers there. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENAULT SAMSUNG TO CUT PRODUCTION ON POSSIBLE LACK OF PARTS FROM JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Renault Samsung Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will reduce production to prepare for a possible lack of auto parts coming from Japan in the wake of earthquakes, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 GM Korea Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering cutting output for the same reason. (published 2347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: TALBOT GROUP PLANS TO SELL ALL ASSETS - SUNDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mining investment company Talbot Group is planning to sell all its investments and has sold a A$190.9 million stake in iron ore explorer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sundance Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Sundance Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 George Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0656 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUTCHISON PORT OPENS AT US$0.975 ON DEBUT VS US$1.01 IPO PRICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Port Holdings Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  made its debut on the Singapore Exchange Friday at US$0.975 a unit, 3.5% below its initial public offer price of US$1.01, in the largest ever listing on the Singapore bourse. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUTCHISON PORT HOLDINGS CHAIRMAN: MINIMAL IMPACT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FROM JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Newly-listed port operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Port Holdings Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that it expects "minimal" impact from Japan's destructive earthquake and tsunami. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREAN AIR\f28 \uc2 \f2  REVISES DREAMLINER CONTRACT; DELIVERY TO START IN 2016 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean Air Lines Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has revised its order for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 787 Dreamliner aircraft and that it would start receiving the new planes from 2016. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ANZ TARGETING 25%-30% PROFIT FROM OVERSEAS BY 2017 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is aiming to generate 25%-30% of its profit from overseas by 2017 and is open to acquisitions, it said in a strategy update on Friday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QANTAS SETTLES WITH NZ AUTHORITIES OVER PRICE FIXING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has reached a settlement with New Zealand authorities in relation to price fixing conduct in its freight division. (published 2309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELSTRA DELAYS VOTE ON NATIONAL BROADBAND NETWORK DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Australia's largest telecommunications provider, said Friday negotiations with state-owned NBN Co. over its part in the development of a A$36 billion national broadband network continue to progress but that it will have to delay a shareholder vote on the deal. (published 2313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUTCHISON PORT MAY SEE TEPID SINGAPORE DEBUT DUE TO IMPACT OF JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Port Holdings Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2 's initial public offering--Southeast Asia's largest ever and the world's biggest so far this year--may see a lackluster debut on the Singapore exchange Friday due to the impact of the destructive earthquake and tsunami that hit Japan. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHALCO: TO BUY REMAINING 9.5% STAKE IN CHINA ALUMINUM INTERNATIONAL FOR CNY115 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aluminum Corp. of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd., also known as Chalco, said Thursday it will buy the remaining 9.5% stake in China Aluminum International Trading Co. that it doesn't already own for CNY115 million. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ZTE: COMPANY HEDGES AGAINST US DOLLAR MORE THAN AGAINST EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 18-03-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese telecommunications equipment maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 ZTE Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . currently hedges more against the U.S. dollar than against the euro, Chief Financial Officer Wei Zaisheng said Friday. (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; TOKYO JUMPS, YEN DROPS ON G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A surge in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's shares led most Asian stock markets higher Friday, as the Group of Seven industrialized nations agreed to a coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to staunch the yen's recent surge, providing some relief as the nation grapples with last week's crippling earthquake and an ongoing nuclear crisis. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CNPC: PETROCHINA SUPPLIES 200,000 TONS OIL PRODUCTS FOR JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . 's Japan unit has secured more than 200,000 metric tons of oil products to aid the quake-stricken country, parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COSMO OIL CHIBA TERMINAL RESUMES VESSEL CARGO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -SHIPPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cosmo Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s oil terminal at the port of Chiba has resumed vessel cargo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and is open for business, marine-service provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inchcape Shipping Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on its website, following a survey of ports. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: TALBOT GROUP PLANS TO SELL ALL ASSETS - SUNDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mining investment company Talbot Group is planning to sell all its investments and has sold a A$190.9 million stake in iron ore explorer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sundance Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Sundance Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 George Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA PRIME MINISTER: JAPAN EVENTS TO PROMPT US TO REVISIT SAFETY STRATEGIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mounting concerns over damaged nuclear reactors in Japan will prompt India to revisit its own nuclear safety strategies, Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Friday, indicating the island nation's trauma will play a significant role in shaping the final framework for handling nuclear accident liabilities in India. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA TO DELAY SHALE GAS BLOCK AUCTION PLAN TO ADDRESS ENVIRONMENTAL CONCERNS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government has put a plan to auction shale gas blocks on hold for about a year, as India's environment ministry has raised concerns over the methods used to extract the natural gas, the Financial Express reported Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA NUCLEAR CAPACITY STILL TO RISE SHARPLY BY 2015 -STATE RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's installed nuclear power capacity is still expected to rise sharply by 2015 despite its decision to temporarily suspend approvals of new projects. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA HANWHA LOOKS TO US, CHINA FOR SOLAR EXPANSION -YONHAP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hanwha Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a privately-controlled South Korean conglomerate, said Friday that it has established a research center in Silicon Valley in the U.S. to develop next-generation solar energy technologies, Yonhap news agency reported. (published 0357 GMT) [ 18-03-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i000gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
