\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 04:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: G-7 PLEDGES RARE JOINT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS CRISIS-STRICKEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SELLS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped yen on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Friday to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's record surge from further damaging an economy ravaged by earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disaster. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN NODA: DOLLAR FALL TO AROUND Y76 TAKEN INTO ACCOUNT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Friday that the dollar's plunge to its all-time low around the Y76 level was taken into account in Japan's decision to seek cooperation from its Group of Seven counterparts in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. (published 0236 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STATEMENT OF G-7 FINANCE MINISTERS AND \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVERNORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We, the G-7 Finance Ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governors, discussed the recent dramatic events in Japan and were briefed by our Japanese colleagues on the current situation and the economic and financial response put in place by the authorities. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BERNANKE, TRICHET FIRST AMONG G-7 CENTRAL BANKERS SAYING WOULD HELP IN YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to curb the value of the yen was unanimously backed by all members of the Group of Seven industrialized nations, with U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet the first in expressing their support for the coordinated move, a G-7 official told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ SHIRAKAWA: BOJ TO CONTINUE TO PROVIDE AMPLE LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to pump cash into Japan's financial system as needed to stabilize domestic financial markets as Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts act jointly to stabilize \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN YOSANO: BOJ WON'T BE ASKED TO TAKE SPECIAL STEPS ON ANY RECONSTRUCTION-RELATED BONDS -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano said Friday that the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't be called upon to take special steps such as underwriting any earthquake reconstruction government bonds, after a local media report earlier in the day said Tokyo had decided on such an option, the Nikkei reported. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: BEHIND YEN'S RECORD SURGE; INDIVIDUAL INVESTORS, HEDGE FUNDS SCRAMBLED TO BUY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A day after a heart-stopping rally drove the Japanese yen to one of its sharpest ascents in history, traders and bankers blamed a freak onslaught of forced buying by Japanese individual investors and hedge funds--a barrage that came at the exact time of day when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is at its most vulnerable. (published 2326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOST CHINA CITIES' FEBRUARY NEW HOME PRICES UP ON MONTH, ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices of newly built homes in 56 of the 70 large and medium-sized Chinese cities covered in a survey rose in February from the previous month, down from 60 cities in January, the country's statistics bureau said Friday, indicating the central government's tightening measures are gradually having an effect. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: EBA: EU STRESS TESTS WILL FOCUS ON BANKS' CORE TIER 1 CAPITAL LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European officials unveiled some details of the "stress tests" they plan to run on the continent's banks, hoping to show that the exercise will be tough enough to defuse fears about the sector's health. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCK FUNDS INVESTING IN JAPAN HAD WEEKLY INFLOW OF $956M - LIPPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock funds investing in Japan had $955.9 million in net inflows for the week ended March Wednesday, said Lipper. (published 2247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF ENGLAND'S DEPUTY GOVERNOR AGAINST IMMEDIATE RATE RISE -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britain has entered a hazardous period as new question marks hang over the domestic economy's recovery at a time of persistently above-target inflation, a top Bank of England official said, The Times in London reported Friday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE CONTINUES TO EVAPORATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumers became even more pessimistic about the outlook for the economy and their job prospects during February, and less willing to spend, according to a monthly survey commissioned by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nationwide Building Society\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN TO REDOUBLE FUKUSHIMA WATER COOLING EFFORTS; RADIATION LEVELS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese officials on Friday plan to redouble efforts to cool overheating spent fuel to prevent radiation leaks at the severely damaged Fukushima nuclear power plant, as slight declines in radiation levels around the plant raised hopes that water-spraying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started Thursday may be having the intended effects. (published 0250 GMT) [ 18-03-11 0301GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0007l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
