\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Fed  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In G-7 Effort; Dollar Clings Below Y81-2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew J. Johnson, Stephen L. Bernard and Bradley Davis Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, buying dollars and selling yen as part of a coordinated effort by Group of Seven nations to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was the first coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000 and started overnight in Tokyo when the Bank of Japan initiated a promised "battle" against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of England, Bundesbank, \uc2 Banque de France\uc2  and Bank of Italy all then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during European trading, and the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  also acted.\par \par \uc2 Nomura Securities estimated Y2 trillion for the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and another $5 billion across Europe. Those coordinated efforts helped send the dollar shooting up as high as Y82 from Y78.93 late Thursday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Fed came right at 8 a.m. EDT, the start of the New York trading day.\par \par \uc2 Traders in New York estimated that orders were placed in mostly $50 million blocks with multiple banks and that the Fed likely traded about $600 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed the world's central banks stood with the BOJ in a coordinated effort to push back against speculators who had ridden down the dollar against the yen to record levels early Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The strength of the yen has been a long-time problem for Japanese officials even before this week, as it makes it difficult for its high-tech and auto components export-driven economy to compete in the global market. Japan's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has contributed to deflationary conditions which have proven hard to shake for the world's third-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The question market participants were asking themselves Friday following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was how long the dollar will remain propped up against the yen, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 One of the reasons why \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been typically frowned upon as a form of market manipulation is that they have typically not worked for long.\par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked to Y81.76 in the first minute of trading in New York, after the Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it then pulled back to trade around Y80.90 the rest of the Friday session.\par \par \uc2 "It's human nature to test the limits, but I do think they will respect this, as they [definitely] provoked a response [on Thursday]," said Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon in New York, about speculators.\par \par \uc2 But Alan Ruskin, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in New York, said there will be "lots of probing of central banks' will power" long-term.\par \par \uc2 Nomura analysts Friday said from the BOJ's perspective an ideal dollar target level is between Y82.70 and Y83.00.\par \par \uc2 As a prelude to Friday, the dollar plunged to a record low of Y76.25 early in Thursday's global session, shattering the previous low of Y79.75.\par \par \uc2 The yen had been strengthening as traders bet Japanese insurers and corporations would need to repatriate yen to help pay for rebuilding the country after last week's major earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the euro also climbed Friday to its highest level this year against the dollar, as traders added to bets on expected interest rate hikes in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began ticking higher after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said the bank was "extremely attentive" on anchoring inflation expectations, a signal that rate hikes could be coming shortly. The euro subsequently rose as high as $1.4185.\par \par \uc2 Late Friday, the euro was at $1.4180 from $1.4020 late Thursday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y80.62 versus Y78.93 late Thursday. The euro was at Y114.34 from Y110.58. The U.K. pound was at $1.6223 from $1.6137. The dollar was at CHF0.9010 from CHF0.8987.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 75.556 from about 75.968. -By Andrew J. Johnson, Stephen L. Bernard and Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3092; andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Javier E. David, Neil Shah and Erin McCarthy contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110319e73i00dyt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
