\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: Asian Summary; Joint G-7 Deal Helps Japan Weaken Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 07:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0557 GMT [Dow Jones] ASIAN SUMMARY: Regional markets are mostly higher, led by the Tokyo market after the G-7 agreed to joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the JPY's recent surge as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggles with multiple natural disasters and an ongoing nuclear emergency. The Nikkei is +2.6%, the S&P/ASX is +1.6%, the HSI is +0.6%, the Kospi is +1.3%, the Taiex is +1.3%, the Shanghai Composite is +0.7% and the STI is +0.3%; the Sensex is 1.0% lower on political concerns after leaked cables. In \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the JPY pulled back sharply after the G-7 pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  dumped yen on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Japan's MOF sold JPY through the BOJ for the first time since September and Japanese finance minister Yoshihiko Noda said each G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its own timezone. The USD/JPY jumped to 81.88 from 78.93 late Thursday in New York, the EUR/JPY is at 115.18 from 110.62 and the EUR/USD is at 1.4070 from 1.4020.\par \par \uc2  China needs to effectively lower the massive amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  it buys to rein in inflation, a professor at PBOC's training institute says. February prices of newly built homes in 68 of the 70 Chinese cities covered by National Bureau of Statistics survey rose on-year. Mounting worries over Japan's nuclear crisis will prompt India to revisit its own nuclear safety strategies, says Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh. Spot gold is at $1,410.40/oz, up $6.40 from the NY close. April Nymex crude oil futures are up $1.40 at $103.26/bbl. (philip.vahn@dowjones.com) Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110319e73i003v7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
