\par\par \b \uc2 DJ G-7 Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  With  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange \highlight\uc2  Market - G-7 Statement\b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors Friday expressed solidarity with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pledged to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ensure orderly markets.\par \par \uc2 'We express our solidarity with the Japanese people in these difficult times, our readiness to provide any needed cooperation and our confidence in the resilience of the Japanese economy and financial sector,' the G-7 said in a statement issued following an emergency meeting to discuss the situation in Japan.\par \par \uc2 'As we have long stated, excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates have adverse implications for economic and financial stability. We will monitor exchange markets closely and will cooperate as appropriate,' it added.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110319e73i000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
