\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Tokyo Shares Up 2.7% As Yen Falls On G-7  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brad Frischkorn Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks rose sharply in early Friday trading after the Group of Seven jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei Stock Average was up 2.7% at 9206.78 about 40 minutes after opening, after an initial surge of as much as 3.0%, with all 33 Topix subindexes in positive territory. The June futures contract lagged the cash market, however, trading up 2.2% at 9130.\par \par \uc2 Trading volumes were robust with about 680 million shares traded thus far, in line with recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Japan's massive quake, tsunami, and nuclear crisis, concerns had grown that the liquidation of overseas assets by insurers and other institutions and repatriation of yen to Japan would be massive. That sent the yen's dramatically higher, to record levels against the U.S. dollar this week. That raised fears that the problems for the Japanese economy would be compounded, as exporters profits could be hammered by the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to as low as Y76.25 in early Asian trading on Thursday, and rebounded to the low Y79-levels by early Friday.\par \par \uc2 After the G-7's announcement, and joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the G-7, which nearly coincided with the Nikkei open, the dollar rose sharply against the yen, and was last at Y81.17.\par \par \uc2 G-7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors expressed solidarity with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pledged to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ensure orderly markets.\par \par \uc2 'We express our solidarity with the Japanese people in these difficult times, our readiness to provide any needed cooperation and our confidence in the resilience of the Japanese economy and financial sector,' the G-7 said in a statement issued following an emergency meeting to discuss the situation in Japan.\par \par \uc2 Most traders had expected that the G-7 would at least allow \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the promise to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more positive than expected, says Yumi Nishimura, deputy general manager at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 Still, any further rise for the Nikkei is likely limited around 9,250, she says, citing continued concerns over the still-unresolved nuclear situation.\par \par \uc2 'The problems at the nuclear plant are far from over, and we have a three-day weekend ahead, so it's hard to keep buying on the weaker yen alone,' she says.\par \par \uc2 Honda Motor\uc2  led major exporters, rising 4.1% at Y3,180. Shares of Tepco, which owns and runs the stricken nuclear facility, were up 10.4% at Y881, after suffering five straight sessions of massive losses.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110319e73i000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
