\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par FED COMPLETES STRESS TESTS OF 19 LARGEST US BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't disclose the test results and doesn't say which institutions were granted permission to increase dividends. The Fed says it will discuss the tests with banks Friday and present them with a more detailed review later this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LIBYA DECLARES CEASE-FIRE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya's foreign minister says the country will abide by the United Nations Security Council resolution calling for military action in Libya, and will implement an immediate cease-fire and end all military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  across the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; BUYS DOLLARS AND SELLS YEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, buying dollars and selling yen as part of a coordinated effort by Group of Seven nations to weaken Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS RISE, FINANCIALS BOOSTED BY DIVIDEND NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks climb as fears of violence in Libya scale back, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  help relieve pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy and a handful of U.S. companies raise their dividends.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL PRICES FLAT ON LIBYA CEASE-FIRE DOUBTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil prices are nearly flat on doubts about Libya's declaration of an immediate cease-fire. Nymex April crude is up a penny at $101.43 a barrel after falling as low as $100.32 earlier after the cease-fire was ordered.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO RADIATION TAD HIGHER THAN NORMAL, IAEA TO MEASURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Radiation levels in the Tokyo area are around typical background levels, while in areas close to the quake-damaged Fukushima nuclear power plant they remain high but still below levels that would pose a threat to human health, officials say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QATAR SENDS TROOPS TO BAHRAIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qatari troops are part of the Gulf forces deployed to Bahrain to put down Shiite-led protests against the Sunni dynasty there, says a Qatari military official.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HIKES BANKS RESERVE RATIO FOR THIRD TIME THIS YEAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says it will raise the share of deposits banks must hold in reserve by 0.50 percentage points, the third hike this year, as inflationary pressures remain in the spotlight.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAI TO SELL YOPLAIT STAKE TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 GENERAL MILLS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French private equity fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 PAI Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it is in exclusive talks with French dairy cooperative \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sodiaal\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Mills\f28 \uc2 \f2  to sell a 51% stake in dairy products maker Yoplait for a little over \u8364\'20\'AC800 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN TRADING DESK CUTS PART OF ANNUAL 5% CULLING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 's plan to hire for its investment management division and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in fast-growing foreign markets like China doesn't mean it has put a stop to an annual ritual that culls the lower 5% of its staff.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CATERPILLAR DEC-FEB GLOBAL DEALER SALES UP 59% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cat's World-wide sales rose 59%, with strong sales growth across all geographic markets, marking the 10th straight rolling three-month period of sales expansion for the company.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  ANALYSIS \par  Brent To Rise On Mideast Unrest, Japan Adds Uncertainty \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil price forecasts have risen drastically amid the Middle East turmoil, analysts surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires say, with some saying that Japan's recent crisis and its impact on the global economy and nuclear energy sector are adding to uncertainty.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  TAKING STOCK \par  Japanese Stocks Were Touted As Cheap Before... \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before the earthquake hit, there were plenty of people who thought Japanese stocks were on offer at bargain-basement prices. Even if you didn't fully agree back then, what about now? David Cottle writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   ============ U.S. MARKETS ACTION =========== \par DJIA              up 105.61 points to 11880.20 \par NASDAQ            up  7.26 points to 2643.31 \par S&P 500           up  8.53 points to 1282.25 \par 10-year T-note    102 30/32 at 3.2749 yield \par NYMEX Crude       down $0.08 at $101.33/bbl \par Dollar/Euro       up 0.1180 at 1.41390 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-18-11 1201ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110318e73i000ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
