\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: Fed  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 ; Buys Dollars and Sells Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds additional details about size of Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in fourth paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Stephen L. Bernard \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, buying dollars and selling yen as part of a coordinated effort by Group of Seven nations to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was the first coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began in Tokyo with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of England, Bundesbank, \uc2 Banque de France\uc2  and Bank of Italy all \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during European trading, and the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Fed came right at 8 a.m. EDT, the start of the New York trading day.\par \par \uc2 Traders estimate that orders were placed in $50 million blocks with multiple banks. That could mean the Fed traded somewhere between $600 million and $1 billion depending on how many of the country's biggest banks it used to execute its trades and whether, as some suggest, some banks were used more than once.\par \par \uc2 The initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Fed was symbolic to show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood with the Bank of Japan in the coordinated effort, said Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York Mellon in New York. But he added that it was also a "warning shot across the bow" of speculators trying to fight the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked to Y81.76 in the first minute of trading in New York, but has since pulled back. It was most recently trading at about Y81.10.\par \par \uc2 Based on the price action, the Fed and \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a more sustained manner, as opposed to a "one-shot deal," said Brian Kim, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Stamford, Conn.\par \par \uc2 "It could be maybe they're going to spread it out," Kim said of measures to curb yen strength. "Or maybe that was it."\par \par \uc2 When all is said and done, the dollar may be propped to Y82, Kim said, which could be a psychologically significant number and would bring the dollar back to pre-earthquake levels.\par \par \uc2 Nomura Securities said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue into next week as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes further attempts to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nomura said the ideal dollar target level is between Y82.70 and Y83.00.\par \par \uc2 The yen had been strengthening as traders bet Japanese insurers and corporations would need to repatriate yen to help pay for rebuilding the country after last week's major earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a record low of Y76.25 early in Thursday's global session, shattering the previous low of Y79.75.\par \par \uc2 The Fed had $11.922 billion worth of yen-denominated assets, as of the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 -By Stephen L. Bernard, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-4528; stephen.bernard@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Bradley Davis, Andrew J. Johnson, Erin McCarthy, Javier David and Neil Shah contributed to this report. [ 03-18-11 1140ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110318e73i000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
